  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "tab-solids",
   "text": "Prisms & cones"
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Explore"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "solid-reset",
   "text": "Reset view"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "solid-intro",
   "text": "Height records time. The bottom is f₀, the top is f₁, and the sides are the boundary motions already chosen."
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Whole boundary"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Bottom · f₀"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Top · f₁"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Sides · earlier H"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": "solid-left-title",
   "text": "A × [0,1] · the domain"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": "solid-right-title",
   "text": "C(A) ⊆ Y · the allowed outputs"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "solid-play",
   "text": "▶ Play"
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Time t0.40"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "solid-hint",
   "text": "Drag the prism to rotate · click its slice to choose x · arrow keys also rotate."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "solid-equation",
   "text": "∂(A × [0,1]) = (A × {0,1}) ∪ (∂A × [0,1])"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "solid-status",
   "text": "Bottom, top, and sides agree where they meet. Together they prescribe a map on the entire boundary."
  },
  {
   "tag": "summary",
   "id": null,
   "text": "What am I looking at?"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "A homotopy H maps the whole cylinder X × [0,1] into Y. For one source piece A, its cylinder A × [0,1] is a prism: an edge gives a rectangle, and a filled triangle gives a solid triangular prism."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "We first prescribe f₀ on the bottom and f₁ on the top. The sides carry the homotopies already constructed on smaller faces. Nesting puts all these outputs in C(A). Contractibility lets us extend the boundary map across the prism while keeping every prescribed value."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "The right-hand picture is one explicit convex example: every face is assigned the same target disk, and H(x,t) = (1−t)f₀(x) + tf₁(x). The height in the left picture is a domain coordinate, not a coordinate in Y."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Carrier proof · pp. 21–22 · Cones · Hatcher, Chapter 0"
  }
 ],
